{
  "provider": "isolved",
  "entity": "deduction_setup",
  "notes": [
    "Candidate setups (D-017): one DeductionSetup per legal-level payItems entry, source_basis candidate_assignment with an unvalidated_source diagnostic, id from (legal, entry id). Each entry is joined to the per-employee payItems entry with the same (legal, employee, id) (7 of 7 live). Only entries whose per-employee payItemType is Deduction are setups; the per-employee route's negative-id entries are catalog placeholders, not setups (D-066).",
    "Join result (D-081): the two routes agree on every field of the 7 joined entries except payItemType (null on the legal list 7 of 7) and calcParams (missing or shorter on the legal list for 2 of 7). So payItemType and calcParams are read from the per-employee entry, the other fields from the legal list.",
    "deduction_code_id from payItemCode joined to the client catalog by code (D-066); 2 of 7 live entries have no code and stay unlinked (null with not_provided). Classification comes from the catalog code (D-047).",
    "calcParams: paramType Amount fills amount; Percent, Amount2 and Rate stay raw in provider_extensions with unit_unverified (scale and meaning undocumented, CANONICAL_MODEL 6.2).",
    "Garnishments: one DeductionSetup per garnishments item, source_basis documented_assignment, category garnishment (from the route, raw_code 'garnishments', CANONICAL_MODEL 1.7), id from (legal, garnishment id). A 404 with an empty body means none (D-011). selectedDeductions keep their provider ids in garnishment.linked_deductions; they are not required to join a pay item (0 of 2 do)."
  ],
